            "patch_url": "https://github.com/reconifyhq/reconify/pull/124.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-21T23:48:15Z"
          },
          "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nThis PR implements the Engine Agent Evaluation Corpus (AP-9) by adding eight small fixture scenarios that exercise the Reconify Engine against external coding agents. \r\n\r\nFollowing the structure discussed in the issue, all scenarios are located under the new `evals/` directory and use the `scenario.json` machine-readable contract format for the future AP-10 cross-agent runner.\r\n\r\nThe 8 implemented scenarios are:\r\n1. `001-missing-payment` (Unmatched left)\r\n2. `002-duplicate` (Duplicate detection)\r\n3. `003-settlement-fee` (Amount tolerance match)\r\n4. `004-timing-difference` (Date window match)\r\n5. `005-one-to-many` (Grouped match via `one_to_many` pass)\r\n6. `006-many-to-many` (Grouped match via `many_to_many` pass)\r\n7. `007-multi-provider` (Multiple right counterparts `[stripe, paypal]`)\r\n8. `008-ambiguous-reference` (Fuzzy matching via `name_mode: tokens`)\r\n\r\nEach scenario contains input CSVs, an agent `prompt.md`, the ideal `reconify.yaml` configuration, and the `scenario.json` assertions file.\r\n\r\n## Related issue(s)\r\n\r\nCloses #109\r\nRelates to #101\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [ ] Bug fix\r\n- [x] New feature\r\n- [ ] Breaking change\r\n- [ ] Documentation\r\n- [ ] Chore / refactor\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] `make preflight` passes\r\n- [x] `make mod-check` passes\r\n- [x] `make fmt-check` passes\r\n- [x] `make lint` passes\r\n- [x] `make security` passes\r\n- [x] `make test` passes\r\n- [x] `make build` succeeds\r\n- [x] `make bench-smoke` passes\r\n- [x] README/examples/docs updated if user-facing CLI or config behavior changed\r\n- [x] No generated benchmark data, local CSVs, coverage files, binaries, or `*.local.yaml` configs committed\r\n",
