          "created_at": "2026-08-21T20:26:39Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-08-21T20:26:39Z",
          "body": "I've gone through all the commits now, and I completely agree with every call you made.\r\n\r\nRegarding Section 5 (Prompts): You are 100% right. If we explicitly tell the agent \"use name_mode: tokens\", we're only testing its ability to translate english to YAML. Rewriting the prompts to describe the business context is the exact right philosophy here, as it forces the agent to actually reason about the reconciliation strategy.\r\n\r\nRegarding Section 6 (Guardrail Rows): This is a brilliant addition. I hadn't considered that an overly permissive config would technically pass the basic assertions. Adding counter_examples/ and explicitly testing them to fail is an incredibly robust way to ensure we're grading for precision, not just completion.\r\n\r\nThe new inputs/, reference/, and expected/ layout also makes the contract much clearer. I have no pushback on any of this. The corpus looks fantastic and the evals_test.go integration is super clean. I'm fully aligned—this is good to merge!",
